column12:
I'm not sure how WooThemes uses this file, but you can require a user to be logged in to access it fairly easily.  This might break some part of WooTheme's functionality.<p>Edit `your-theme/functions/js/shortcode-generator/preview-shortcode-external.php`<p>Somewhere below the `require_once( $url . '/wp-load.php' );` line:<p><pre><code>   if(!is_user_logged_in())
   {
       wp_die(__('Nope'), __('Nope'), array('response' => 403));
   }
</code></pre>
If you happened to move your wp-content directory[1] this exploit is not going to work on you.  The `require_once` statement above relies on wp-content existing so it can find `wp-load.php`<p>1. <a href="http://codex.wordpress.org/Editing_wp-config.php#Moving_wp-content" rel="nofollow">http://codex.wordpress.org/Editing_wp-config.php#Moving_wp-c...</a>
